ioned his vision  of people putting on an oculus vr  headset and doing things like studying  in a classroom of students and teachers  all over the world  or consulting a doctor face to face  just by putting on goggles in your own  home but during the phase of the  acquisition  oculus fans and supporters were  extremely upset  about facebook buying them out even  saying that they're done with oculus  because of the deal so the founder of  oculus headed to reddit  and personally guaranteed that users  would not need to log into their  facebook account  every time they want to use their oculus  rift well  unfortunately in 2018 facebook required  users to link  their facebook and oculus accounts  together in order to access oculus  venues and then just last year facebook  began  forcing oculus owners to log into their  facebook account  basically breaking the initial promise  that the founder of oculus made and  going even deeper  back in 2014 he promised that they  wouldn't track users  flash ads at them or do anything  invasive  well in 2019 facebook announced that  they will now  track your vr data to make ads more  relevant  if you're logged into facebook which  they now obviously require  and just to give you an idea of what  they're tracking here's all of the data  that facebook would capture  about your vr use also including your  voice activities  moving on in june of this year oculus  announced that they began to test  in headset vr advertisements something  that they promised  they would not do and if you're  wondering why facebook would do this  well it turns out that according to  steam's hardware survey  oculus vr headsets now make up over  60 percent of the total vr headset usage  on steam  with the most recent oculus quest 2  headset taking up  a massive 31 alone  with by far the fastest growth of almost  1  over the past month in fact facebook  says that the quest 2  has already outsold every previous  oculus headset combined  and it did it in its first 